# Modular Components — No God Components or God Hooks

Do not build large monolithic components or a single feature hook that owns every query, mutation, and handler. Split UI into small, focused files. Each file should have one responsibility; **the component that renders an action owns that action.**

Works together with [`no-callback-props.mdc`](no-callback-props.mdc): do not lift handlers into a parent (or parent hook) and pass them down as props.

## Core rules

1. **One logical concern per file.** A save footer, upload tile, gallery row, and delete confirmation are separate components.
2. **API interactions at the lowest level.** Mutations, queries, and cache invalidation live in the component that triggers or displays them — not in a parent and not in a shared `useFeatureEverything()` hook.
3. **Colocate with the owning route or feature.** Keep UI under `_components/` at the lowest owning App Router segment (see [`nextjs-app-file-organization.mdc`](nextjs-app-file-organization.mdc)).
4. **Use folder hierarchy for semantic grouping.** Multi-part features get their own folder; nest `components/` (or domain-specific subfolders) when several leaves belong to one shell.
5. **No `index.ts` / `index.tsx` barrels.** The entry file is named after the feature (e.g. `recipe-header/recipe-header.tsx`); imports use that explicit path — see [`no-component-index-files.mdc`](no-component-index-files.mdc).

**Examples in this rule are illustrative only.** Adapt names and structure to the product.

## Complex features (dialogs, wizards, multi-section panels)

For flows with several actions (save, upload, delete, generate, etc.):

| Layer | Responsibility |
| ----- | -------------- |
| **Feature folder** | Groups all files for one dialog, panel, or screen section |
| **Thin shell** | Layout, dialog chrome, composition of sections — no mutations |
| **Section / leaf components** | Own their UI, handlers, and API hooks |
| **Feature context** (when needed) | Shared *UI state* only (`open`, draft selection, item pending delete) — not shared handlers |
| **Sync helper** (optional) | Small effect-only module to align shared state with external inputs (e.g. reset draft when dialog opens) |

### Folder layout (illustrative)

```
_components/
  recipe-composer/
    recipe-composer-image-dialog/
      recipe-composer-image-dialog.tsx          # shell + provider wrapper
      recipe-composer-image-dialog-context.tsx  # shared UI state
      recipe-composer-image-dialog-sync.tsx     # optional effects (no UI)
      build-ai-image-prompt.ts                  # pure helpers
      components/
        recipe-composer-image-dialog-footer.tsx # Save / Cancel + save mutation
        upload-recipe-image-tile.tsx            # Upload + create/confirm mutations
        delete-image-alert-dialog.tsx           # Delete + delete mutation
        previously-used-images-section.tsx      # List query + gallery
        previously-used-image-card.tsx          # Select + open delete flow
```

### Anti-patterns

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — one hook owns every action and query; shell only wires props
function useImageDialog() {
  const upload = useCreateMediaUpload();
  const deleteAsset = useDeleteMediaAsset();
  const handleSave = () => { /* ... */ };
  const handleUpload = () => { /* ... */ };
  return { handleSave, handleUpload, /* 20 more fields */ };
}

function ImageDialog() {
  const dialog = useImageDialog();
  return (
    <Footer onSave={dialog.handleSave} />
    <UploadTile onUpload={dialog.handleUpload} />
  );
}
```

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — each leaf owns its behavior; context holds shared selection only
function UploadRecipeImageTile() {
  const { setPendingAssetId } = useRecipeComposerImageDialog();
  const createUpload = useCreateMediaUpload();
  const handleUploadFile = async (event: ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) => {
    // mutation + setPendingAssetId here
  };
  return (/* file input + tile */);
}

function RecipeComposerImageDialogFooter() {
  const { pendingAssetId, setOpen } = useRecipeComposerImageDialog();
  const { setValue } = useFormContext();
  const handleSave = () => {
    setValue('imageAssetId', pendingAssetId);
    setOpen(false);
  };
  return (/* Cancel + Save buttons */);
}
```

## Shared state between siblings

When multiple cousins need the same UI state (pending selection, which row is being deleted, dialog open):

- Prefer a **feature-scoped React context** or **Jotai atoms** scoped with a `Provider` at the feature root.
- Store **values** (`pendingId`, `assetToDelete`, `open`), not **callback bundles**.
- For cross-cutting guards (e.g. block dialog close while upload runs), expose minimal flags from context (e.g. register busy keys from the component that owns the mutation) — do not centralize the mutation in the provider.

Layout-only parents may compose children with **no props** beyond `children` or static labels.

## Leaf component with its own data

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — the component that shows the data owns the fetch
export function SummaryMetrics() {
  const { data } = useQuery({
    queryKey: ['reporting', 'summary'],
    queryFn: fetchReportingSummary,
  });

  if (!data) return null;

  return (
    <section>
      <Metric label="Total" value={data.total} />
    </section>
  );
}
```

## Checklist before adding a feature hook

- [ ] Does this hook only hold **shared UI state** or **derived read-only** values? → OK in context / small hook file.
- [ ] Does it call **mutations** or define **submit/upload/delete/save** handlers used by multiple children? → Split into the components that render those controls.
- [ ] Am I passing `onSave`, `onUpload`, `onDelete`, etc. through props? → Move handlers into the child that has the button (see [`no-callback-props.mdc`](no-callback-props.mdc)).
